{"page_content": "Data source What it tells us Surface Tension If the surface tension of an aqueous solution is less than 10 mN/m, the substance is a surfactant and this will enhance the potential dermal uptake. Surfactants can also substantially enhance the absorption of other compounds, even in the absence of skin irritant effects. Skin irritation / Corrosivity enhance penetration. Dermal toxicity Signs of systemic toxicity indicate that absorption has occurred. However, if data steps have not been taken to prevent grooming, the substance may have been ingested and therefore signs of systemic toxicity could be due to oral rather than dermal absorption. Skin sensitisation If the substance has been identified as a skin sensitiser then, provided the data challenge application was to intact skin, some uptake must have occurred although it may only have been a small fraction of the applied dose. Trace elements (<1%). Stable or radio-isotopes should be used and background levels determined to prevent analytical problems and inaccurate recoveries.", "metadata": {"doc_id": "4e2b6bd0-12c8-4271-be66-4a664aaaaf77", "content_type": "Table", "filename": "information_requirements_r7c_en.pdf"}}